      "message": "Tested on a Nokia 7.1 (LineageOS 23.2) with a Youfone SIM (MVNO on KPN, 204-08): the \"ims\" APN from this change works for Youfone too, IMS registers with KPN\u0027s P-CSCFs and VoLTE calls work both ways.\n\nYoufone still can\u0027t attach to LTE with this change alone, though. With the wildcard types gone, no 204-08 entry serves \"ia\", so the attach uses the first \"default\" entry, AH Mobiel Internet (protocol IP). Youfone on KPN LTE only grants IPv6 bearers (ONLY_IPV6_ALLOWED), so the attach fails and the phone ends up emergency-only (KPN has dropped 2G for Youfone, cause 11). I\u0027ve uploaded https://review.lineageos.org/c/LineageOS/android_vendor_apn/+/508549 for that: it matches the Youfone entries on SPN, gives Youfone Internet the \"ia\" type and adds a Youfone IMS entry. It doesn\u0027t depend on this change.",
